From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI/DPC: only enumerate the DPC service on ports that can use AER

97ca178c899d ("PCI/DPC: Allow DPC on all Downstream Ports when OS controls
AER") made get_port_device_capability() advertise PCIE_PORT_SERVICE_DPC for
any port that has a DPC capability as soon as the host bridge has native AER
(host->native_aer), dropping the previous per-port AER test.  dpc_probe()
still declines such a port with -ENOTSUPP when pcie_aer_is_native(pdev) is
false, which for a port without an AER *capability* is always the case:

    if (!pcie_aer_is_native(pdev) && !pcie_ports_dpc_native)
            return -ENOTSUPP;

On Apple T2 Macs (Intel Cannon Lake PCH, e.g. MacBookPro16,1) the chipset
root ports expose DPC but are not AER-capable, so every boot logs an
error-level line per port:

    dpc 0000:00:1b.0:pcie008: probe with driver dpc failed with error -524
    dpc 0000:00:1c.0:pcie008: probe with driver dpc failed with error -524

(-524 is -ENOTSUPP.)  DPC is not enabled on those ports either way: the
service device is created, the probe declines, and the device is left
unbound, so nothing is lost by not creating it.

Gate the DPC service on the same condition dpc_probe() needs: the port must
have an AER capability so pcie_aer_is_native() can be true.  The
pcie_ports=dpc-native override deliberately allows DPC without AER ownership
and is preserved.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie/portdrv.c b/drivers/pci/pcie/portdrv.c
index a9cbfc1..00127ba 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie/portdrv.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie/portdrv.c
@@ -264,7 +264,8 @@ static int get_port_device_capability(struct pci_dev *dev)
 	 */
 	if (pci_find_ext_capability(dev, PCI_EXT_CAP_ID_DPC) &&
 	    pci_aer_available() &&
-	    (pcie_ports_dpc_native || host->native_aer))
+	    (pcie_ports_dpc_native ||
+	     (host->native_aer && dev->aer_cap)))
 		services |= PCIE_PORT_SERVICE_DPC;
 
 	/* Enable bandwidth control if more than one speed is supported. */
